WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.868
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.100
You're here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.501
That's what I'm talking about.
I love it.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:11.234
Well, let's get to some news.
Everybody is talking about this.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:14.234
The U.S. has examined recovered
pieces of the Chinese

00:00:14.234 --> 00:00:16.801
spy balloon, and today they
announced that it had

00:00:16.801 --> 00:00:19.934
technology to monitor
our communications.

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:21.567
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.634
When they heard that,
Siri and Alexa were like,

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.434
"Oh, hell no, that's our job.
Come on."

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.300
Yeah, they were tracking
all of our communications,

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.834
including phone calls
and text messages.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:34.501
The balloon was like,
"Based on what we've gathered,

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.000
we should invest in eggplants."

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:46.567
[ Applause ]

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:49.501
Meanwhile, AT&amp;T told their
customers, "Relax, they can't

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:50.901
spy on you
if you can't get a signal."

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.434
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.968
Some more news, President Biden
just said

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:58.701
the classified documents found
at his home and office

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.701
were from the 1970s.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.267
Yep, they were mostly about
trying to determine

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.934
the exact location of Funkytown.

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.100
♪♪

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.534
Some more news on the President.
In a new interview ahead of

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:16.000
his expected re-election
campaign, Biden dismissed

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.501
concerns about his age and said,
"Watch me. It's all I can say."

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:23.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.367
Then someone was like, "Sir,
you're talking to a mannequin."

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.434
He's like, "Oh, I'm sorry."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.367
Listen, I'm not saying he's old,

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:33.033
but Biden actually ate the
original Werther's Original.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.734
Does that make sense?

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:40.634
Actually, Vice President Harris
expressed her confidence

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:44.367
in Biden, calling him a very
bold and vibrant president.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:45.801
Bold and vibrant.

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:49.067
Sounds like something you say
when you're asked to describe

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.567
a wine but you don't know what
you're talking about.

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:54.234
You're like, "Bold.
I'm getting a lot of vibrant."

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:56.434
Bold and vibrant.
It's always good when you

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:59.067
describe a president the way
Sephora describes a lipstick.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.400
Did you guys see this?
Today, a top Southwest Airlines

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.400
executive testified before
Congress

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.501
over the holiday travel
meltdown.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.434
And just to mess with him,
right when he showed up

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:10.901
for his hearing,
Congress canceled it.

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:14.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.000
Yeah, he said the problem is
solved,

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.067
but I'm not sure I believe him.

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:18.834
He flew to D.C. on JetBlue.

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:23.033
Well, guys, the Super Bowl is
just a few days away.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.667
Are you guys excited about it?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.133
I'm excited.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:30.367
I'm looking forward to it.
As you've probably heard by now,

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:33.767
two brothers, Travis and Jason
Kelce, are playing against

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.434
each other in this Sunday's
Super Bowl.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.400
So their mom, Donna Kelce,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.334
has been in the news
a lot this week.

00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:40.767
And here she is right here.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.634
I saw that -- I know. How cute.

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:44.567
It's like a mixed jersey.
I love it.

00:02:44.567 --> 00:02:47.467
So, I saw that Donna packed her
homemade chocolate chip cookies

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.634
for her boys in Arizona
and sent it to them.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:50.968
Check this out.
This is a photo of them.

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:52.968
Isn't that cute?
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:52.968 --> 00:02:55.334
She wrote their names and "love,
Mom" on the Tupperware.

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.100
Yeah, classic mom move.
I love that.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.267
Well, she also sent cookies
to other people as well.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:01.834
-Did she really?
-Yeah, first Donna sent cookies

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:03.534
to Tom Brady and wrote...

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:08.167
-Wow!
-Nice.

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.167
-Sweet, so sweet.
-Then she sent cookies to

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.634
Rob Gronkowski and wrote...

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.601
Then she sent cookies
to Olivia Manning,

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.834
the mother of Peyton and Eli,
and wrote...

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:27.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.133
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:32.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.067 --> 00:03:34.601
Then she sent cookies to Rihanna
and wrote...

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:39.501
[ Laughter ]
You can't. She's taken. Yeah.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.734
And finally, she sent cookies
to Patrick Mahomes and wrote...

00:03:43.868 --> 00:03:45.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.834
Nice lady.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.567
-Spicy cookies.
-Well, listen to this.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.734
King Charles just became the
first monarch in British history

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:56.100
to be featured on postal stamps
without a crown.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.367
-Ohh!
-Can we see the photo?

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:00.367
Yeah. There you go.

00:04:00.367 --> 00:04:02.100
It looks like a sad dime.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:09.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.000
People complained he should be
wearing a crown.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.501
Charles was like, "Oh, lick me."

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:14.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.267
"I'm a stamp.
I'm a postage stamp."

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.767
Some big movie news, Disney just
announced that they're working

00:04:19.767 --> 00:04:22.701
on sequels to "Toy Story"
and "Frozen."

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:24.968
Yeah, Prince Harry heard
the words "frozen" and "woody"

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.234
and had a traumatic flashback.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.067
-Put a crown on it.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.501
-Well, get this, in an effort
to fill seats, I heard that

00:04:33.501 --> 00:04:37.567
movie theaters are offering more
upscale food and drink options.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:40.067
It's weird when a waiter comes
to your seat with nacho cheese

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.367
and is like, "Say when."

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:45.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:47.100
There's even a sommelier
that you can beckon over.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.501
Like, "What wine pairs well with
'Knock at the Cabin'?"

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:50.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:52.033
Something bold and vibrant.

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.934
People are excited about this.
Chick-fil-A is debuting

00:04:55.934 --> 00:04:57.901
a new fried cauliflower
sandwich.

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.400
[ Audience cheers ]

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.467
People say it really tastes like
chicken if you just add

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.300
a little salt, pepper,
and chicken.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.634
Well, guys, as I mentioned,
the Super Bowl is almost here,

00:05:08.634 --> 00:05:10.200
and it seems like everyone is
looking forward to

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.667
Rihanna's halftime show.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:17.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:17.901 --> 00:05:21.033
I got to say, people online have
some pretty wild thoughts

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:23.067
about what song she might do.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:26.901
I'm sure whatever she does is
going to work, work, work, work

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:29.801
because she's just too good
of a performer.

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:32.234
Anyone who says different is
just being rude.

00:05:32.234 --> 00:05:34.701
Boy, girl, everyone loves her.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:35.968
Yeah, I said it.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.868
She's performing live, and she's
under a lot of pressure.

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:42.367
I mean, sure there's a delay of
about four, five seconds,

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:45.100
but still, anyway, make sure you
get a good seat

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:48.234
for the halftime show
where no one will disturb ya.

00:05:48.234 --> 00:05:51.634
I'll tell you, if anyone at
my party isn't paying attention,

00:05:51.634 --> 00:05:53.734
they can shut up and drive to
their own house

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:57.334
because the monster performance
she's about to give,

00:05:57.334 --> 00:05:59.801
she's the only girl in the world
that can do it.

00:05:59.801 --> 00:06:02.634
When you think about it, she's
just what the game needed.

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:06.734
Me? I'm just hoping they don't
stop the music.

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:09.067
Can you imagine if there were
sound issues?

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:11.701
I mean, you'd send out an S.O.S.
to fix that problem.

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.334
But I'm sure it will be
just fine.

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:16.434
So from me to you, Riri,
whatever you grace us with,

00:06:16.434 --> 00:06:19.000
just know that everyone at the
game will be telling each other

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.534
how you run this town.

00:06:20.534 --> 00:06:22.467
And when you're done,
take a bow.

00:06:22.467 --> 00:06:24.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.634
Umbrella.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:30.033
♪♪

00:06:30.033 --> 00:06:31.367
Finally,
I'm very excited about this.

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:33.133
Super Bowl LVII
is happening this Sunday.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.400
You have
the Philadelphia Eagles...

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.567
...facing off against
the Kansas City Chiefs.

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:39.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:42.601
Now, as you know,
after the game,

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.300
they give out awards
like Most Valuable Player,

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.133
but they also give out awards
before the game, too.

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:47.434
Did you know that?
-No, I did not.

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:49.000
-Yeah, they do.
I'll show you what I mean.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.534
It's time for
"Tonight Show Superlatives."

00:06:50.534 --> 00:06:52.400
Here we go.

